# Web Dev Team Onboarding

Hello, my name is **Sera (@cellsera\_c on Discord)**, and I am the **Team Leader for the Web Dev Team**!


## What We Do

The Web Dev team is responsible for implementing and maintaining the various websites that the project hosts.

Before continuing with this doc, please read the General Onboarding Document [here](https://docs.p3dual.com/guides/onboarding/).

Currently, the project has 2 repositories:


### [p3d-web](https://github.com/p3d-project/p3d-web)

P3D Web is designed to act as the primary gateway for the project, serving as the main distribution point for project updates.

It is built on the [Astro](https://astro.build/) framework with [React](https://react.dev/) components and [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/) to leverage fast static-site generation and responsive, utility-driven design.


### [p3d-docs](https://github.com/p3d-project/p3d-docs)

P3D Docs is the official documentation website. It serves as the main distribution point for all project docs, including team setup & codebase references.

Engineered for high performance and long-term maintainability, it is built on the [Astro](https://astro.build/) framework with [React](https://react.dev/) components and [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/) to leverage fast static-site generation and responsive, utility-driven design.


### [elizabeth-bot](https://github.com/p3d-project/elizabeth-bot)

Elizabeth Bot is a bespoke Discord onboarding and application management bot built for the P3D Project that streamlines the applicant workflow.


## Contributions

Before contributing, please read our [**Git Guidelines**](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VFd1PVnq54xNJtYytFMzO0MBaeUISCHVfw2-U37n3Lw/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.d81vadwf1qp1). Any contributions that do not follow these guidelines will **NOT be accepted**!

The process of assigning tasks is self-directed. You'll need to select a task from the [GitHub Project Board](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=repo%3Ap3d-project%2Fp3d-web+or+repo%3Ap3d-project%2Fp3d-docs+or+repo%3Ap3d-project%2Felizabeth-bot) under **“Ready”** & assign yourself & assign yourself. Sometimes, team leads will ask you to do some issues as well.

Once you have finished, please share photos/videos/PR of the completed issue to the #web-lounge for feedback. Once we've given the OK, you can upload the files to the Web team’s folder in [Google Drive](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1lmywpQcTfiyInSn9x-1sV79dSRKNSFSE?usp=sharing) (if relevant).

Make sure that you strictly follow the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing). If you want to work on an issue that isn’t on the roadmap, make sure you get approval from the team lead (cellsera\_c) or the project lead (thebosst). If you want to work on an issue that IS on the [Roadmap](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VUxY2xVGtKzGWCES0VeZ_-vMpKSifB5vTW2ZkXJMPJM/edit?usp=sharing), find the associated GitHub issue! If you can’t find it, feel free to make a new issue under the “New” tab.

All new Web team members must also read [Web Dev Team Reference](https://docs.p3dual.com/references/web-dev-team-reference/) & [Art Standards](https://docs.p3dual.com/references/art-standards/)


## AI Usage Policy

The usage of AI tools is permitted **if used responsibly,** to be more precise under these conditions:

- You designed the core idea. AI can help you implement or refine it, not invent it for you.

- You understand it. If you can't explain what the code does, it doesn't belong in a PR.

- No slop. Generated code must be clean, logical, and intentional.


